        {
          "id": "tensor-core",
          "parent": "smem",
          "name": "Tensor Core (3rd gen)",
          "group": "compute",
          "color": "#2a58b8",
          "geom": { "type": "box", "size": [0.7, 0.35, 0.9], "pos": [-1.25, 0.5, -0.55] },
          "repeat": { "count": [4, 1, 1], "step": [0.83, 0, 0] },
          "desc": "Multiplies matrix tiles per warp instruction (mma.sync). First Tensor Core generation to add TF32 (no code changes needed for FP32 training) and structured fine-grained sparsity.",
          "specs": [
            {
              "label": "Precision formats",
              "value": "FP64, TF32, BF16, FP16, INT8, INT4",
              "source": "https://www.nvidia.com/content/dam/en-zz/Solutions/Data-Center/a100/pdf/nvidia-a100-datasheet-us-nvidia-1758950-r4-web.pdf"
            },
            {
              "label": "Structured sparsity",
              "value": "2:4 fine-grained sparsity — up to 2x throughput (e.g. BF16 312 → 624 TFLOPS)",
              "source": "https://www.nvidia.com/content/dam/en-zz/Solutions/Data-Center/a100/pdf/nvidia-a100-datasheet-us-nvidia-1758950-r4-web.pdf"
            }
          ],
          "role": "tensor-core"
        },
        {
          "id": "register-file",
          "parent": "smem",
          "name": "Register file",
          "group": "memory",
          "color": "#d07a40",
          "geom": { "type": "box", "size": [0.7, 0.25, 0.9], "pos": [-1.25, 0.45, 0.55] },
          "repeat": { "count": [4, 1, 1], "step": [0.83, 0, 0] },
          "desc": "Per-thread registers. Tensor Core accumulators live here (no separate tensor-memory on Ampere).",
          "specs": [
            { "label": "Size (per SM)", "value": "256 KB (4 × 64 KB)", "estimate": true }
          ],
          "role": "register-file"
        },
        {
          "id": "warp-scheduler",
          "parent": "register-file",
          "name": "Warp scheduler + CUDA cores",
          "group": "control",
          "geom": { "type": "box", "size": [0.7, 0.15, 0.9], "pos": [-1.25, 0.75, 0.55] },
          "repeat": { "count": [4, 1, 1], "step": [0.83, 0, 0] },
          "desc": "Each cycle picks a ready warp (32 threads) to issue. Scalar CUDA cores (FP32/INT32) run the epilogue: bias, activation, quantization.",
          "role": "warp-scheduler"
        },
        {
          "id": "async-copy",
          "parent": "smem",
          "name": "Async copy (cp.async / LDGSTS)",
          "group": "io",
          "geom": { "type": "box", "size": [1.6, 0.15, 0.4], "pos": [-0.9, -0.25, 1.4] },
          "desc": "New in Ampere: the cp.async instruction (LDGSTS) copies data straight from global memory (L2/HBM) into shared memory without passing through registers or the L1 miss path. On Volta, a thread had to load a value into a register before storing it to shared memory, burning registers and round-trip latency for every tile element. Hopper later replaced this with a dedicated TMA hardware unit issued by a single thread for whole tensor tiles.",
          "specs": [
            {
              "label": "vs Volta (V100)",
              "value": "Removes the register round-trip for global→shared copies; overlaps copy with compute",
              "source": "https://www.nvidia.com/content/dam/en-zz/Solutions/Data-Center/a100/pdf/nvidia-a100-datasheet-us-nvidia-1758950-r4-web.pdf"
            }
          ],
          "role": "async-copy"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "flows": [
    { "id": "hbm-left", "from": "hbm-dram-left", "to": "die", "group": "memory", "particles": 2 },
    { "id": "hbm-right", "from": "hbm-dram-right-active", "to": "die", "group": "memory", "particles": 2 }
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "1. Weights sit in HBM2e: 80 GB across 5 active stacks (of 6 package sites), ~2 TB/s aggregate.",
      "focus": ["hbm-dram-left", "hbm-base-left", "hbm-dram-right-active", "hbm-base-right-active", "hbm-site-inactive"],
      "dot": "hbm-dram-left",
      "explode": 0.6,
      "drill": null,
      "stage": "hbm"
    },
    {
      "text": "2. Memory controllers on each side read their attached HBM2e stacks.",
      "focus": ["mc-left"],
      "dot": "mc-left",
      "stage": "memory-controller"
    },
    {
      "text": "3. Data lands in the 40 MB L2 cache, split into two 20 MB partitions.",
      "focus": ["l2-left", "l2-right"],
      "dot": "l2-left",
      "stage": "l2"
    },
    {
      "text": "4. cp.async (LDGSTS) copies A/B tiles straight from L2/HBM into shared memory — new in Ampere, bypassing registers; V100 needed a register round-trip for the same copy.",
      "focus": ["async-copy"],
      "dot": "async-copy",
      "drill": "sm-detail",
      "stage": "async-copy"
    },
    {
      "text": "5. Tiles sit in the 192 KB L1/shared memory, ready for the Tensor Cores.",
      "focus": ["smem"],
      "dot": "smem",
      "drill": "sm-detail",
      "stage": "shared-memory"
    },
    {
      "text": "6. A warp issues mma.sync: the 3rd-gen Tensor Core multiplies the tile in TF32 or BF16.",
      "focus": ["tensor-core"],
      "dot": "tensor-core",
      "drill": "sm-detail",
      "stage": "tensor-core"
    },
    {
      "text": "7. With structured 2:4 sparsity, the Tensor Core skips zeroed weights and roughly doubles effective throughput.",
      "focus": ["tensor-core"],
      "dot": "tensor-core",
      "drill": "sm-detail",
      "stage": "sparsity"
    },
    {
      "text": "8. Partial sums accumulate in the register file; steps 4–8 repeat along K.",
      "focus": ["register-file"],
      "dot": "register-file",
      "drill": "sm-detail",
      "stage": "accumulate"
    },
    {
      "text": "9. Epilogue: CUDA cores add bias, apply activation, quantize.",
      "focus": ["warp-scheduler", "register-file"],
      "dot": "warp-scheduler",
      "drill": "sm-detail",
      "stage": "epilogue"
    },
    {
      "text": "10. Results go back to HBM; with tensor parallelism, NVLink 3 (600 GB/s) all-reduces with other GPUs.",
      "focus": ["nvlink"],
      "dot": "nvlink",
      "drill": null,
      "stage": "writeback"
    },
    {
      "text": "11. MIG can slice the SMs, L2 and memory controllers into up to 7 isolated GPU instances for multi-tenant serving.",
      "focus": ["sm-a", "sm-b", "gigathread"],
      "dot": "gigathread",
      "drill": null,
      "stage": "mig"
    }
  ],
